# Chocolate Chip Oatmeal Cookies

Based on [A Nestle Recipe](https://www.nestleprofessional.us/recipe/choc-oat-chip-cookies) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20250517024926/https://www.nestleprofessional.us/recipe/choc-oat-chip-cookies))

{ rating="5" image="chocolate_chip_oatmeal_cookies.jpg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### (1) In a medium bowl, whisk

- [ ] 1.75 cups [all-purpose flour]{ ing="all-purpose-flour" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [baking soda]{ ing="baking-soda" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }

### (2) In a large bowl, combine

- [ ] 1 cup (2 sticks) [butter]{ ing="butter" }, softened
- [ ] 1/2 cup [granulated sugar]{ ing="granulated-sugar" }
- [ ] 1.25 cup [brown sugar]{ ing="brown-sugar" }, packed

### (3) Then

- [ ] 2 tsp [vanilla extract]{ ing="vanilla-extract" }
- [ ] 2 Tbsp [milk]{ ing="milk" }
- [ ] 2 large [eggs]{ ing="egg" }
- [ ] 2.5 cup [quick or old-fashioned oats]{ ing="quick-or-old-fashioned-oats" }
- [ ] 2 cups (12 oz) [chocolate chips]{ ing="chocolate-chips" }

## Recipe

1. Soften [butter]{ ing="butter" } at room temperature
1. Preheat oven to 375F
1. In a small bowl, combine [flour]{ ing="all-purpose-flour" }, [baking soda]{ ing="baking-soda" }, and [salt]{ ing="salt" } (1)
1. In a large mixing bowl, combine [butter]{ ing="butter" } and [sugars]{ ing="brown-sugar" } until creamy using a hand mixer (2)

   1. Add [vanilla extract]{ ing="vanilla-extract" } and [milk]{ ing="milk" }
   1. Add [eggs]{ ing="egg" } one at a time beating well
   1. Beat in [flour]{ ing="all-purpose-flour" } gradually
   1. Stir in [oats]{ ing="quick-or-old-fashioned-oats" } and morsels
1. Measure out rounded Tbsp of dough on a light colored ungreased baking sheet
1. Bake 9-11 minutes until golden brown. Cool on a wire rack

## Notes

1. Pan Cookie Variation: Grease 15 x 10-inch jelly-roll pan. Prepare dough as above. Spread into pan. Bake for 20 to 25 minutes or until golden brown. Cool in pan on wire rack. Makes 4 dozen bars
1. Also see the main cookie recipe: [Chocolate Chip Cookies](./chocolate_chip_cookies.html)
1. Other oatmeal cookie variations: [Soft & Chewy Oatmeal Raisin Cookies](./soft_chewy_oatmeal_raisin_cookies.html), [Dark Chocolate Cranberry Oatmeal Cookies](./dark_chocolate_cranberry_oatmeal_cookies.html)
